    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Cloquet/Administrator-5---Executive-Human-Resources-Officer_JR0000005682": {
      "title": "Administrator 5 - Executive Human Resources Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Administrator 5 - Executive Human Resources Officer Institution: Fond du Lac Tribal and Community College Classification Title: MnSCU Administrator 5 Bargaining Unit / Union: 220: Minnesota State Administrator's Plan City: Cloquet FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $91,507.00 - $146,527.00 Job Description: The Executive Human Resources Officer provides vision, leadership, and strategic direction for the human resources activities of the college, overseeing the recruitment, training, development, and engagement of talent for all divisions of the institution. Responsibilities include the administration of personnel and labor relations policy for classified and unclassified administrators, managers, faculty, professional, clerical, and maintenance employees; adherence to collective bargaining agreements; recruitment, and onboarding processes for all positions; employee engagement and performance management; leadership and staff training and development; classification, compensation, and benefits administration; HRIS systems administration; and supervision of the Human Resources office. Principles of diversity, affirmative action, and equal employment opportunity will be applied to all college human resources practices. This position involves significant discretion and substantial involvement in the development, interpretation, and implementation of college policy. This position provides confidential advice to the president and administrative team. Salary Range: $91,507 - $127,994 Annually Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business, Public Administration or related field. Five (5) or more years of progressively responsible professional Human Resources experience. Knowledge of labor relations, employment law, and HR best practices. Demonstrated leadership, communication, and relationship-building skills. Commitment to diversity, equity, inclusion, and shared governance. Ability to manage confidential and complex employee relations matters. Preferred Qualification  Master’s degree in related field. Society for Human Resource Management (SHRM) certification or Human Resource Certification Institute (HRCI) certification. Human Resources leadership experience in higher education or the public sector. Experience administering collective bargaining agreements and working with unions. Strategic planning, organizational change, and workforce planning experience. Experience leading a comprehensive Human Resources function, including recruitment, employee relations, compensation, benefits, and organizational development. Other Requirements Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Monday - Friday 8:00 am - 4:30 pm Telework (No) - Telework is not available About The mission of Fond du Lac Tribal and Community College is to provide higher education opportunities for its communities in a welcoming, culturally diverse environment.   To achieve this mission, we will: ·          Promote scholarship and academic excellence through transfer and career education and provide access to higher education by offering developmental education. ·          Respectfully promote the language, culture, and history of the Anishinaabeg. ·          Provide programs which will celebrate the cultural diversity of our community and promote global understanding. ·          Promote a sense of personal respect and wellness. ·          Provide technological opportunities and experiences, preparing students for the future. ·          Provide programs and baccalaureate degrees that fulfill our commitment to American Indian communities, our land grant status, and the union of cultures.   Vision Statement Fond du lac Tribal and Community College offers a postsecondary education to honor the past, for those living in the present and dreaming the future, through a spirit of respect, cooperation, and unity.   Core Values During 2013 and 2014, Fond du Lac Tribal and Community College identified five core values to be used as guiding principles on campus. Our core values are: ·          Respect: Manaaji’idiwin ·          Integrity: Gwayakwaadiziwin ·          Stewardship: Ganawenjigewin ·          Innovation: maamamiikaajinendamowin ·          Compassion: Zhawenjigewin Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 12-14-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 09-03-2026 Close Date: 10-01-2026 Posting Contact Name: LeAnn K Ulvi Posting Contact Email: leann.ulvi@fdltcc.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/St-Cloud/Associate-Director-of-Honors-College--MSUAASF-Range-C_JR0000005686": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Honors College- MSUAASF Range C",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted Today\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Associate Director of Honors College- MSUAASF Range C Institution: St. Cloud State University Classification Title: MSUAASF Range C Bargaining Unit / Union: 211: Minnesota State University Association of Administrative Service Faculty City: St. Cloud FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $47,845.00 - $93,809.00 Job Description This position coordinates and administers comprehensive academic advising, operational processes including efforts to publicize the program and support recruitment, and student success initiatives within the Honors College. The role supports the academic progress, engagement, and   timely   degree completion of Honors students through integrated advising, data-informed program support, and cross-functional collaboration. Additionally, the position contributes to institutional retention and student success goals by   facilitating   effective program operations, supporting fiscal and administrative processes,   leveraging   data to inform continuous improvement, and coordinating work across multiple academic and administrative functions to support institutional student success goals. The role   operates   with independent judgment in managing daily functions while aligning work with institutional policies, program standards, and strategic priorities.     Responsibilities and Results   Student Success, Advising, and Belonging – 30%   Provide proactive, developmental academic advising to Honors students, supporting academic planning, degree progression, and successful navigation of university requirements.   Evaluate requests for exceptions to Honors program requirements and determine   appropriate resolutions   consistent with policy, precedent, and student circumstances.   Design and implement student success and retention initiatives that promote academic excellence, community building, and students’ sense of belonging.   Interpret university policies, curriculum requirements, and Honors program standards to guide student decision-making.    Monitor student progress,   identify   risk factors, and implement   timely   interventions that support retention, persistence, and   timely   degree completion.   Maintain   accurate   advising documentation and student records in institutional systems.   Apply individualized advising strategies to meet diverse student needs.   Serve as primary advisor to the University Honors Club, supporting student leadership development and engagement.   Coordinate and support signature Honors community ‑ building activities and events, such as first ‑ year and transition programming, retreats,   showcases , and recognition activities.   ​ Program Coordination and Operations – 15%   Coordinate Honors College program processes, including onboarding, curriculum tracking, and graduation verification.   Manage day ‑ to ‑ day operational workflows, resolving issues and ensuring continuity of services.    Collaborate with faculty and staff to support effective delivery of Honors programming.   Support implementation and consistency of program requirements in alignment with institutional and Minnesota State standards.   Mentor and supervise student employees and graduate assistants, including training, delegation of responsibilities, and performance feedback.   Plan and coordinate medium-complexity projects and events involving multiple campus partners, timelines, and resource requirements.   Evaluate operational processes and implement workflow improvements that enhance efficiency, compliance, and student service outcomes.   Resolve complex student, program, and operational issues requiring interpretation of university and Honors College policies and coordination across multiple offices.   ​ Data Management and Assessment – 15%   Develop,   maintain , and analyze data related to student participation, progression, and outcomes.   Generate reports and dashboards to support program evaluation and decision-making.   Maintain   accurate   records of student progress, Honors requirements, engagement, and outcomes using institutional data systems and technologies.   Identify   trends in student data to inform   advising   strategies, program improvements, and resource considerations.   Design and implement assessment projects and evaluation tools to measure student engagement, retention, learning, and program effectiveness.   Translate assessment findings into recommendations for annual priorities, student success initiatives, and program improvements.   ​ Fiscal Operations,   Purchasing , and Compliance – 20%   Assist   with budgeting and fiscal operations, including monitoring and evaluating multiple budget units, tracking expenditures, and ensuring alignment with approved allocations.   Support annual and ongoing budget planning processes by compiling financial data, projecting needs, and adhering to university, Minnesota State, and state policies.   Process and track purchasing activities, including requisitions, reimbursements, and vendor transactions, ensuring accuracy and compliance with procurement guidelines.   Coordinate student   worker   payroll processes, including timesheet verification, appointment tracking, and adherence to payroll policies and timelines.   Participate in the planning, monitoring, and allocation of operational resources to support student success and to ensure compliance with institutional policies, system requirements, and state regulations,   identifying   and resolving discrepancies.   Maintain documentation and internal controls that support transparency, accountability, and audit readiness.   ​ Communication, Collaboration, and Recruitment – 20%   Engage with faculty, academic departments, and student services to coordinate support for Honors students.   Serve as a key point of contact for program information, ensuring clear,   accurate , and consistent communication across stakeholders.   Lead and support Honors College recruitment efforts, including outreach to prospective students, participation in admissions events, presentations, and communications designed to promote program opportunities and benefits.   Represent the Honors College in recruitment and outreach initiatives, collaborating with Admissions and campus partners to support enrollment goals.   Develop and deliver recruitment communications and materials tailored to diverse student audiences.   Collaborate across units to support integrated student success strategies and resolve cross-functional issues.   Participate in committees or workgroups   representing   Honors College needs and priorities.   Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and 3 years of related professional experience in student engagement, advising, or higher education coordination; or   Master’s   degree and one year of related professional experience in student engagement, advising, or higher education coordination    Demonstrated ability to use technology to manage workflow and communications. Demonstrated success in building supportive relationships with students that contribute to student engagement, persistence, and sense of belonging in a higher education setting   Experience using student data and relationship-based practices to   identify   student needs and implement interventions that improve student outcomes and retention   Knowledge of   advising   theory, policy interpretation, and data use   Experience supporting fiscal operations, including budget monitoring,   purchasing   processes, and adherence to institutional and regulatory compliance requirements   Ability to work with students from culturally diverse backgrounds   Preferred Qualification  Master’s degree in higher education, student affairs, counseling, or a related field   Demonstrated experience designing and implementing student success, retention, or engagement initiatives   Experience using data analytics, dashboards, or assessment tools to inform program improvement and student success strategies   Experience contributing to or leading assessment efforts, including developing reports and applying findings to practice   Demonstrated ability to coordinate programs or events that support student engagement, leadership development, and community building   Knowledge of honors education, experiential learning, or undergraduate enrichment programming   Experience managing budgets or financial accounts in a higher education or public sector environment   Experience supervising student employees or graduate assistants   Other Requirements ​ ​ Working conditions are primarily on campus. Some travel, including occasional overnight travel, may be   required   to other sites for events or activities. Some evening and weekend work will be   required . ​     ​ ​ Activities are performed in an environmentally controlled office setting subject to extended periods of sitting,   keyboarding   and manipulating a computer mouse;   required   to stand for varying lengths of time and walk moderate distances to perform work. Lifting/moving presentation and/or marketing materials, up to 40 pounds, may be   required . ​   Please note that successful applicants must be eligible to work in the United States on or before the effective date of appointment. Eligibility includes being a U.S. citizen or national, a lawful permanent resident, or a foreign national authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for employer sponsorship. Employees must maintain work authorization without sponsorship for the duration of their appointment. Documents Needed to Apply Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) 8:00am-4:30pm Monday-Friday About St. Cloud State University serves close to 10,000 students and is committed to providing accessible, high-quality education that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Located along the Mississippi River in St. Cloud, Minnesota, SCSU combines personalized support, applied learning, research, and community engagement to create opportunities for students, employees, and the region. With more than 133,000 alumni worldwide, SCSU continues to make a lasting impact through education, innovation, and service. St. Cloud State University is committed to creating an inclusive and welcoming environment that values the unique contributions of all students, faculty, staff, and community members. We recognize that welcoming a variety of perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds strengthens our teaching, learning, research, and service mission. We encourage applications from individuals who share our commitment to student success, belonging, and excellence. Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for the Minnesota State University Association of Administrative and Service Faculty (MSUAASF) which can be found at: https://www.msuaasf.org/ St. Cloud State University is committed to excellence and actively supports cultural diversity. To promote this endeavor, we invite individuals who contribute to such diversity to apply, including minorities, women, LGBTQIA+, persons with disabilities and veterans. St. Cloud State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, marital status, status with regards to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or status as a U.S. veteran. The Interim Title IX coordinator at St. Cloud State University is Andrea Rooney. For additional information, contact the Office of Institutional Equity & Access, (320) 308-5123, Admin. Services Bldg. Rm 121  Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 10-01-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 09-04-2026 Close Date: 09-18-2026 Posting Contact Name: Courtney Marie Graber Posting Contact Email: courtney.graber@stcloudstate.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/RIDG---Willmar-Campus/Accounting-Officer_JR0000005592": {
      "title": "Accounting Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Accounting Officer Institution: Ridgewater College Classification Title: Accounting Officer Bargaining Unit / Union: 214: Minnesota Association of Professional Employees City: RIDG - Willmar CampusHutchinson FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Classified - Unlimited Salary Range: $24.40 - $35.30 Job Description This position will perform fiscal management functions and accounting work for Ridgewater College by providing leadership in accounting reconciliation processes, compliance monitoring, financial reporting, financial transaction processing (banking, purchasing, disbursement, payroll, grants, etc.) This position applies knowledge in accounting to provide financial management analysis, consultation and training for the college. Principle Responsibilities include: Financial management of grants (federal, state, private), projects, and agreements. Maintain chart of accounts to reflect accurately the cost of grant/project operations. Monitor the financial data throughout the grant/project period ensuring expenses are within parameters of grant/project. Provide required financial reports, complete reimbursement requests for federal and state grants and submit to grantor and assist grant director with close-out requirements including audit. Prepare invoicing per grant/interagency agreements. Reconcile special allocations and grants with SWIFT to ensure accuracy. Provide accounting services to ensure lease agreements, PSEO contracts and college revenue activities are accurate and completed according to deadlines. Determine cash flow assistance and monitor appropriations and the year-end closing of all appropriations. Regularly review and monitor: Provide budget summary and detail reports monthly and upon request. Interpret and audit budget reports, provide details, identify discrepancies and initiate the appropriate correction. Determine, initiate and communicate the appropriate action to resolve issues; this may include a journal entry, expenditure correction, purchasing adjustments or a budget revision. Ensure expenditures are properly recorded in Minnesota State Accounting System within the guidelines of Ridgewater College, Minnesota State and State of Minnesota policies and procedures. Perform other duties as assigned to ensure the smooth functioning of the department and maintain the reputation of the organization as a viable business partner. Salary Range: $24.40- $35.30 /hourly ::: $50,947 -$73,706/annually Minimum Qualifications Two years of work-related experience.  A Bachelor's degree may substitute for 12 months, and an Associate's degree may substitute for 6 months. Skilled in accounts receivable and computerized billing systems, with the ability to accurately enter, access, and correct financial data. Experienced in accounting systems, capable of querying and compiling records, preparing reports, and supporting the development of spending plans, financial status updates, and budget requests. Knowledge of basic accounting procedures, ensuring compliance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) and maintaining precise, complete financial records. Skilled in analyzing, interpreting, reconciling, and preparing financial information; adept at identifying discrepancies and recommending effective solutions to procedural or fiscal issues. Ability to interpret and explain accounting and related fiscal policies, procedures, and practices to customers Knowledge of business practices, principles, and protocols as applied to disbursements, purchasing and receipts techniques Preferred Qualification  Associate’s degree in Accounting, Business, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to organize, prioritize, and perform effectively under pressure while meeting deadlines with accuracy; adaptable to acquiring new skills and knowledge as responsibilities evolve. Familiarity with ISRS, MnSCU Accounting, Workday, Microsoft Office Suite, credit card systems, State of Minnesota eServices (DOR collections), and Perceptive Content. Hands-on experience with document management systems, including setup and ongoing maintenance (e.g., Perceptive Content). Competence in developing and documenting procedures, recommending best practices, and revising processes in response to changing requirements and technologies. Commitment to fostering inclusivity, with demonstrated knowledge of and interest in diverse cultures and populations. Proven ability to maintain confidentiality and handle sensitive information with discretion. Other Requirements Applications Must Include: Resume Cover Letter Additional Requirements In accordance with the Minnesota State Colleges & Universities (MnSCU) Vehicle Fleet Safety Program, employees driving on college/university business who use a rental or state vehicle shall be required to conform to MnSCU’s vehicle use criteria and consent to a Motor Vehicle Records check. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Monday – Friday, 8:00AM-4:30PM Telework (Yes/No) No, this position is not telework or remote About Institution Information MISSION : Ridgewater College empowers diverse learners to reach their full potential and enrich their lives through personalized and relevant education in an accessible, supportive, and inclusive environment. VISION: Ridgewater College is a student-centered educational leader focused on innovation, excellence and affordability. GUIDING PRINCIPLES: Enterprising - We are future-focused, and change-oriented, developing creative solutions to challenges that maximize our institutional, system and local resources. Empowerment – We develop and empower employees to make decisions to best serve students and stakeholders. Excellence – We strive to exceed expectations in all that we do. Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion – We seek to understand and appreciate the needs and experiences of every individual and actively work to provide genuine opportunities for everyone to succeed and participate in college activities and processes. Trust and Respect – We are committed to developing a culture based in processes and behavior that create trust and respect among all stakeholders. Collaboration – We connect and work together to achieve common goals while respecting needs and interests of stakeholders. Curiosity and Creativity – We constantly strive to understand, learn, change, and improve. Accountability – As individuals and groups, we willingly accept and take ownership of our successes and failures. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 10-07-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 08-26-2026 Close Date: 09-18-2026 Posting Contact Name: Felicia Mary Telecky Posting Contact Email: felicia.telecky@ridgewater.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Brooklyn-Park/Military-and-Veteran-Services-Coordinator--School-Certifying-Official_JR0000005641": {
      "title": "Military and Veteran Services Coordinator, School Certifying Official (MnSCU Academic Professional 2)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Military and Veteran Services Coordinator, School Certifying Official (MnSCU Academic Professional 2) Institution: North Hennepin Community College Classification Title: MnSCU Academic Professional 2 Bargaining Unit / Union: 214: Minnesota Association of Professional Employees City: Brooklyn Park FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Unlimited Academic Salary Range: $26.12 - $37.91 Job Description This position provides leadership, coordination, and specialized support for all military-connected students at North Hennepin Community College (NHCC), including Veterans, current service members, and eligible dependents. The individual serves as the institution’s primary School Certifying Official (SCO) and subject matter expert on federal, state, and institutional education benefits related to military service. As the Military and Veteran Services Coordinator, the position also leads programming and services that support enrollment, retention, engagement, community integration, and overall success of military-connected students. The role plays a key part in cross-departmental coordination with Admissions, Advising, Financial Aid, Registration, Student Services, and Accounting/Fees to provide holistic support. This position independently interprets and applies complex policies, ensures compliance with federal and state regulations, and builds strong campus and community partnerships to advance the success and sense of belonging of military-connected students. This position is an active member of the Student Life department. Salary Range: $26.16 - $37.91 hourly Minimum Qualifications A minimum of two years (2) of professional experience. An associate’s degree may substitute for six (6) months of experience, a bachelor’s for twelve (12) months, or a master’s for eighteen (18) months. Ability to work with a diverse population of students, staff, and faculty. Experience and/or training related to serving military-connected individuals and addressing their unique needs and barriers to resources Experience and/or training in data collection and management Demonstrated ability to collaborate across multiple departments/functional areas Strong communication, interpersonal, and problem-solving skills to effectively advise students and coordinate services Ability to interpret and apply federal and state regulations, institutional policies, and benefit guidelines Preferred Qualification  Master’s degree in higher education, student affairs, counseling, public administration, or a related field Two or more years of direct experience working with military-connected students in a higher education setting; demonstrated understanding of their educational barriers and benefits navigation in higher education In-depth knowledge of VA education benefits (e.g., Chapters 30, 31, 33, 35, 1606), DoD Tuition Assistance, and/or the Minnesota GI Bill Prior experience serving as a School Certifying Official (SCO) Experience using Minnesota State information systems/CRM such as ISRS, Workday, and Slate Demonstrated success developing and delivering programming or services for underserved and non-traditional student populations Experience advising students on the coordination of military education benefits with financial aid, academic planning, and/or institutional policies Other Requirements Application must include: Letter of interest Resume Work Shift Monday - Friday 8:00 am - 4:30 pm Telework One day per week depending on the department's need. About Why Choose NHCC? Choose to work at North Hennepin Community College (NHCC), and you will be joining a vibrant and diverse professional community that believes in the power of education to change lives. NHCC welcomes its students and values its employees. NHCC has a rich tradition of excellence in teaching and learning. Founded in 1966, the college is a respected, thriving comprehensive community college with a strong history of liberal arts education and career programs. NHCC is one of the largest and most diverse community colleges in the State of Minnesota. NHCC is a member of Minnesota State which is the fourth-largest system of state colleges and universities in the United States and the largest in the state with 26 colleges, 7 universities and 54 campuses. Offering more than 70 academic programs to over 7,000 students NHCC prepares students to transfer or for immediate entry into the workforce. The thriving campus is also home to a wide variety of student clubs and organizations supporting a largely part-time student body with co-curricular and recreational activities. Join our NHCC community and help us create opportunities for students to reach their academic goals, succeed in their chosen professions, and make a difference in the world. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 10-19-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 08-28-2026 Close Date: 09-21-2026 Posting Contact Name: Michelle Lynn Kiffmeyer Posting Contact Email: michelle.kiffmeyer@nhcc.edu"
    },
