    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Rosemount/General-Repair-Worker_JR0000005647": {
      "title": "General Repair Worker",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: General Repair Worker Institution: Dakota County Technical College Classification Title: General Repair Worker Bargaining Unit / Union: 202: AFSCME - Craft, Maintenance, and Labor City: RosemountInver Grove Heights FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Classified - Unlimited Salary Range: $27.24 - $31.35 Complete Application Requirement — Please Read Before Applying To be considered for this position, applicants must submit a complete application. Applications missing required documents will be marked incomplete and will not advance to review. Job Description Dakota County Technical College (DCTC) seeks a General Repair Worker to perform general repairs, preventative maintenance, and mechanical repairs to building components, physical plant systems, energy management systems, auxiliary generators, college equipment, plumbing, and utilities. This position also assists with minor construction projects, remodeling, and related facility support activities throughout the DCTC campus, including the main building and Power and Chiller Plant. Responsibilities include: Make minor repairs and adjustments to plumbing, electrical wiring, HVAC systems, refrigeration equipment, and college equipment. Complete repairs to mechanical equipment and identify and correct equipment malfunctions. Repair and adjust furniture, shelving, doors, windows, locks, ceilings, and walls. Paint walls, ceilings, doors, floors, and equipment. Assist with minor construction, remodeling, and carpentry projects. Assist with various groundskeeping and landscaping duties, including mowing and snow removal. Operate and maintain trucks, tractors, and other grounds maintenance equipment. Assist with event setup and other campus support activities. Perform custodial duties as assigned. Comply with applicable safety policies, procedures, and licensing requirements. This position is primarily at Dakota County Technical College, but will serve as a back up to Inver Hills Community College. Salary Range: $27.24 - $31.34/Hour; $56,877 - $65,459 /Year Minimum Qualifications ( Must be reflected in application). Knowledge of general methods and practices of a variety of trade areas (e.g. mechanics, masonry, welding, electrical, plumbing and carpentry) sufficient to assist licensed trades workers and to repair machinery, tools and facilities in a timely and safe manner. Knowledge of occupational hazards and safety measures related to trades work sufficient to safely and efficiently perform the job duties. Ability to safely use hand and power hand tools. Ability to safely operate and maintain trucks, tractors, and other ground and road maintenance equipment. Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Ability to provide work instructions to unskilled helpers. Ability to perform physically demanding tasks such as lifting, carrying and bending. Physical Requirements Ability to safely use hand tools, power tools, ladders, lifts, and scaffolding. Ability to work indoors and outdoors in varying weather conditions. Ability to move throughout work sites, including uneven terrain, stairways, and elevated work areas. Ability to position oneself as needed to perform maintenance and repair work in a variety of environments. Ability to perform physically demanding tasks, including material handling, excavation, pushing, pulling, reaching, and moving equipment and supplies weighing up to 50 pounds. Preferred Qualification  Possess or have the ability to obtain a valid Boiler License. Ability to keep simple records and perform assigned tasks with limited work direction. Other Requirements In accordance with the Minnesota State Vehicle Fleet Safety Program, employees driving on college/university business who use a rental or state vehicle shall be required to conform to Minnesota State's vehicle use criteria and consent to a Motor Vehicle Records check. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Tuesday - Saturday; 7:00am - 3:30pm On-call rotation, call back for campus emergencies, and weather emergencies Telework (Yes/No) No.   Application Procedure: The required documents listed below must be included in your application to be considered for initial review. Current Resume: Resume must include dates of employment (month and year) for each position and Indicate average hours worked per week for each job. Cover Letter:  (Optional) Transcript (Optional) Internal Applicants: All current Minnesota State employees will need to log into Workday to apply for the position via the Jobs Hub. The Jobs Hub can be found under the Menu, in the upper left-hand corner of Workday, under the Apps, and then Jobs Hub.  Employees may also search for “Browse Jobs – Employees” in Workday via the search bar at the top to view open positions. External Applicants Applicants not currently employed by Minnesota State can access the  career site  to search and apply for jobs, and to check the status of applications. Those applying for a position will be prompted to create a profile in Workday. This does include other state of Minnesota employees who work for agencies other than Minnesota State. Contact: If you have questions about this position or are in need of a reasonable accommodation during this search process, please contact Human Resources at hr@dctc.edu  or at 651-423-8411. If you experience any issues while submitting your application or creating an account please contact careers@minnstate.edu  for assistance. To receive consideration as a Connect 700 Program applicant, apply online, email the Job ID#, the Working Title and your valid Proof of Eligibility Certificate by the closing date to hr@dctc.edu .  Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: We are a proud equal opportunity and affirmative action employer, and we seek applicants with deep connections to the cultural communities to which our students belong. As an affirmative action employer, we actively seek and encourage applications from women, people of color, persons with disabilities, and individuals with protected veteran status. About: Dakota County Technical College is focused on outstanding education for employment that emphasizes hands-on learning, serving students with a wide variety of diploma and degree programs. Many graduates enter the workforce right away, while others continue their education by transferring to four-year colleges or universities. DCTC is also a leader in noncredit and customized training, working with businesses to improve the skills of their employees. DCTC serves the local community by enhancing economic prosperity for students, their families, and regional businesses. DCTC is aligned with Inver Hills Community College. Located nine miles apart, Inver Hills offers a broad range of liberal arts and professional programs that complement programs at DCTC. Both Dakota County Technical College and Inver Hills Community College are recognized as a Beyond the Yellow Ribbon employers offering support for veteran and military employees and students. In accordance with the Clery Act, prospective employees may review the Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports for Inver Hills Community College and Dakota County Technical College at https://www.inverhills.edu/about/departments/security/security-reports/ and https://www.dctc.edu/support-services/campus-security/security-reports-clery-act /. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 09-23-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 09-01-2026 Close Date: 09-01-2026 Posting Contact Name: Julia Glenn Posting Contact Email: julia.glenn@inverhills.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/St-Paul/Trade---Technical-Education-Office-and-Administrative-Specialist-Sr---Office---Admin-Special-Senior_JR0000005659": {
      "title": "Trade & Technical Education Office and Administrative Specialist Sr - Office & Admin Special Senior",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 2 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Trade & Technical Education Office and Administrative Specialist Sr - Office & Admin Special Senior Institution: Saint Paul College Classification Title: Office & Admin Specialist Sr Bargaining Unit / Union: 206: AFSCME - Clerical and Office City: St. Paul FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Classified - Unlimited Salary Range: Job Description Job Summary: This position exists to provide high-level administrative support to a large, complex college academic division and provides support to the dean and the faculty in this department. This position is responsible for managing complex administrative activities including: managing faculty and classroom schedules with the curriculum management system; budget development and maintenance; and providing detailed information and assistance to the department(s) students. This position serves as the office manager for the Career and Technical division and is responsible for the communication to the entire division serving students, faculty and the deans. This position will also provide administrative support to all of the Advisory Committee meetings for the division. All employees of Saint Paul College are responsible for promoting a culture that supports diversity and inclusion in all forms as well as providing excellent customer service continuously to all internal and external contacts. Job Duties: Provide high level administrative support to the Dean of the Career and Technical Education Division. Manage department’s Curriculum Management System. Serve as office manager for a large, complex academic department(s).  Provide lead work to work study students. Provide administrative support to the Division’s Program Advisory Committee Meetings. Perform other duties as assigned to ensure the smooth functioning of the department and maintain the reputation of the organization as a viable business partner. Salary Range: The salary range for this position is $22.62 - $30.62 hourly. Minimum Qualifications Strong written communication skills sufficient to write, prepare, and edit materials such as memos, procedures, reports, presentations, and other documents that are grammatically correct, in proper format, and are free of spelling errors, explaining complex technical ideas and procedures to varied technical and non-technical audiences. Knowledge of computer software programs for word processing, spreadsheets, and databases sufficient to create, modify and protect files. Customer service practices and principles sufficient to identify customer needs and provide prompt and accurate information in a professional manner in person, over the phone and in writing. Ability to develop, modify, evaluate, improve, and explain administrative and program policies, practices and procedures. Accounting/budgeting/expense reporting skills sufficient to apply protocols to invoices, receipts and purchase orders. Knowledge of using office productivity applications such as Microsoft Office or similar software, maintain calendars and e-mail, file sharing and document collaboration and presentation/meeting technology such as videoconferencing. Knowledge of math sufficient to add, subtract, multiply and divide numbers, use fractions, decimals, and calculate percentages, and use simple formula. Preferred Qualification  Three years of experience as an administrative assistant in an academic setting; Proficiency with advanced features of Microsoft Office Suite (Word, PowerPoint, Access and Excel). Knowledge of the college’s mission and strategic plan; Thorough knowledge of ISRS (Integrated Student Reporting System) and ImageNow is imperative for troubleshooting and resolving issues; Previous experience with meeting and event planning; Familiarity with Minnesota State accounting procedures; Demonstrated ability to work independently and take the initiative to do a job without regular help and advice from others, and direct work activities to achieve work area goals. Ability to multi-task in a fast paced, high-volume environment. Ability to handle detailed information and 100% follow-through on those details; Ability to make decisions on student records processing based on the functions of ISRS and college policies; Demonstrated commitment to diversity and affirmative action principles. Knowledge of office practices and equipment sufficient to develop and improve work procedures and form. Thorough knowledge of faculty workload credit and pay databases like FWM which is imperative for tracking and maintaining faculty overloads and correct pay calculations. Required Application Materials:    Please ensure you have the following items submitted with your application:  Resume/CV Other Requirements Applicant resumes and cover letters should address the minimum and preferred qualifications for this position. If your skills match the required skill for this position, the department may contact you. Reference checks will be conducted for all finalists. This may include a review of documentation related to job performance and education and contact with the finalist current and/or   previous   employers. Applicant must   be authorized to   work for any employer in the United States. We are unable to provide sponsorship or take over sponsorship of employment visas at our institution. The successful candidate under U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services regulations must be able to accept work in the U.S. by the day employment begins. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Monday - Friday, 8:00 AM - 4:30 PM Telework (Yes/No) This position requires in person work from Monday - Thursday with telework opportunities available on Fridays. About S aint Paul College was established in 1910, and we are proud to be honoring education for more than a century.  SPC-Quick Facts . Saint Paul College is committed to supporting diversity in all of its forms. Applicants representing diverse backgrounds are encouraged to apply. We are an equal opportunity, affirmative action employer, and encourages application from underrepresented groups. Recognized as a   Beyond the Yellow Ribbon  employer offering support for veteran and military students. A member of the Minnesota State Colleges and Universities system.  Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 10-21-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 09-02-2026 Close Date: 09-15-2026 Posting Contact Name: Mykayla R Crockett Posting Contact Email: mykayla.crockett@saintpaul.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/St-Cloud/Strategic-IT-Communications---Executive-Operations-Specialist-Communications-Specialist-2_JR0000005626": {
      "title": "Strategic IT Communications & Executive Operations Specialist-Communications Specialist 2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Strategic IT Communications & Executive Operations Specialist-Communications Specialist 2 Institution: St. Cloud State University Classification Title: Communications Specialist 2 Bargaining Unit / Union: 214: Minnesota Association of Professional Employees City: St. Cloud FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Classified - Unlimited Salary Range: $29.76 - $43.69 Job Description This position serves as the university’s strategic leader for IT communications, responsible for developing and executing enterprise communication strategies that support institutional priorities, protect the university’s reputation, and build trust with internal and external stakeholders. Reporting to the Vice President for Technology Strategy & CIO, the role provides leadership and guidance on messaging, stakeholder engagement, and change management for technology initiatives and critical issues.   The position leads communication efforts for complex and high-profile situations, including major IT incidents and cybersecurity events, ensuring clear, consistent, and effective messaging. It also supports the successful execution and visibility of IT priorities through coordinated planning, stakeholder collaboration, and oversight of key meetings and events.   Additionally, this role enhances leadership effectiveness by supporting the CIO and IT leadership through coordination of priorities, workflows, and decision-support activities, ensuring alignment and progress across initiatives. Overall, the position integrates strategic communications and operational coordination to strengthen the impact and visibility of Information Technology Services while advancing the university’s mission.     PRINCIPLE RESPONSIBILITIES AND RESULTS     1. IT Communications Strategy, Advisory, and Crisis Communications: Develop, lead, and continuously refine comprehensive IT communications strategies that support institutional priorities, protect the university’s reputation, and ensure clear, consistent, and effective messaging across all technology initiatives and incidents. Partner with the CIO, IT leadership, and campus stakeholders to define communication goals, messaging, target audiences, and approaches, including advising on change management, stakeholder engagement, and risk mitigation. Establish standards and best practices for IT communications, and oversee the development, review, approval, and delivery of content across appropriate channels. Lead the development and execution of crisis communications for major IT incidents, ensuring timely, accurate, and transparent information while maintaining stakeholder trust and aligning with university policies and regulatory requirements. Anticipate and prepare for potential communication challenges, including media inquiries, and provide strategic guidance to leadership during high-profile or sensitive situations. Apply audience segmentation, message testing, and data-informed analysis to improve communication strategy, strengthen engagement, enhance consistency, and ensure IT messages are clear, timely, accessible, and aligned to stakeholder needs. Ensure IT communications align with institutional messaging and remain clear, accurate, discoverable, and mission focused.     2. IT Meetings, Events, and Special Projects Marketing & Coordination: Plan, lead, and execute meetings, events, marketing efforts, and special projects of varying scope and complexity, including large-scale, high-visibility events with 1,000 or more participants. Ensure successful outcomes through comprehensive planning, proactive coordination, and strategic promotion that drives awareness, engagement, and participation. Identify and engage appropriate stakeholders, establishing clear roles, expectations, and communication approaches to support alignment and successful execution. Develop and manage comprehensive project and marketing plans, timelines, and task tracking, proactively identifying dependencies, risks, and resource needs. Anticipate potential challenges and implement mitigation strategies to ensure continuity, quality, and strong participation. Design and coordinate campaign planning and content and engagement analysis to promote events and initiatives, including audience identification, messaging alignment (in coordination with IT communications), and selection of effective channels to maximize reach and engagement. Oversee all logistical and operational aspects, including venue coordination, technology setup, vendor engagement, catering, registration, and on-site execution. Ensure all arrangements are completed accurately and on time, while maintaining flexibility to adapt to changing needs or priorities. Prepare and coordinate materials to support event and project success, including agendas, presentations, briefing documents, notes, signage, and participant communications. Ensure a consistent, professional experience that reflects institutional standards and enhances the visibility and impact of IT initiatives. Continuously evaluate event, marketing, and project outcomes, incorporating feedback and lessons learned to improve processes, effectiveness, and stakeholder satisfaction over time.     3. IT Executive Operations & Communications Specialist: Support IT leadership effectiveness by enabling coordination, visibility, and follow ‑ through on strategic priorities, initiatives, and communications. Organize and track leadership work efforts, timelines, and interdependencies in support of departmental and university goals, using lightweight, Agile ‑ informed practices such as work tracking, prioritization support, and status reporting to promote alignment and consistent progress. Maintain a comprehensive understanding of organizational context, competing priorities, key stakeholders, and relevant technologies and industry trends impacting the department. Apply this knowledge to provide strategic analysis, planning support, and actionable recommendations to the CIO and ITS leadership. Develop and deliver clear, audience ‑ appropriate communications that support leadership initiatives and decision-making, including presentations, briefings, status updates, and messaging for internal and external stakeholders. Partner with IT leaders and campus stakeholders to ensure alignment of messaging, proactively engage stakeholders, and translate complex technical concepts into accessible, actionable information. Anticipate communication needs, triage inquiries, and ensure timely, accurate, and consistent information flow across leadership and stakeholder groups. Coordinate meetings, stakeholder engagement efforts, and follow-up actions to ensure alignment, accountability, and progress on key initiatives. Continuously assess effectiveness of coordination and communication approaches, incorporating feedback and adapting practices to improve clarity, efficiency, and leadership impact.     4. IT Executive Enablement: Enable leadership and department effectiveness by providing effective high-level executive support to the CIO. Manage a complex and dynamic executive calendar by aligning schedules with evolving priorities, anticipating conflicts, and making informed decisions to optimize leadership time and focus. Coordinate scheduling logistics with internal and external stakeholders, ensuring professionalism, discretion, and responsiveness. Prepare and organize meeting agendas, briefing materials, and supporting documentation to ensure leaders are well-prepared for decision-making and engagement. Coordinate travel, approvals, and administrative processes while independently resolving issues and ensuring seamless execution of day-to-day operations. Triage inquiries, proactively researching and addressing issues that fall outside established processes. Build and maintain strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders, representing the CIO and IT organization with professionalism, discretion, and sound judgment across all interactions.     5. IT Administrative Process Management and Data Stewardship: Analyze, develop, implement, and continuously improve administrative processes to ensure efficiency, effectiveness, and alignment with departmental and institutional priorities. Evaluate existing workflows, identify opportunities for improvement, and implement solutions that enhance consistency, compliance, and operational performance. Manage the collection, organization, storage, and distribution of documents and records, both physical and electronic, in accordance with department procedures, institutional policies, Minnesota State system requirements, and applicable local, state, and federal laws, regulations, and industry standards. Serve as the data custodian for ITS, ensuring appropriate handling, access, retention, and protection of information assets. Perform and oversee administrative functions that support operational continuity, including maintaining organizational records (e.g., organizational charts), preparing documentation, and coordinating information resources.   Minimum Qualifications Two (2) years of professional-level experience in communications, public relations, marketing, or a related field. A Bachelor's degree may substitute for one year of experience; an Associate's degree may substitute for six months of experience.     Experience developing and implementing communication strategies and plans.   Demonstrated experience writing, editing, and delivering communications for diverse audiences.   Experience translating complex or technical information into clear, audience-appropriate communications.   Demonstrated ability to build effective working relationships with stakeholders and cross-functional teams.   Experience managing communications projects, initiatives, or campaigns.   Strong organizational, communication, and technology skills.   Preferred Qualification  Experience supporting information technology, digital transformation, or enterprise-wide communications.   Experience developing and executing crisis communications or issues management strategies.   Experience advising leaders on communication strategy and stakeholder engagement.   Experience supporting organizational change management initiatives.   Experience planning and executing events, campaigns, or outreach efforts.   Experience applying project management principles and tools.   Ability to manage multiple priorities, work collaboratively, and achieve results in a fast-paced environment.   Other Requirements Please note that successful applicants must be eligible to work in the United States on or before the effective date of appointment. Eligibility includes being a U.S. citizen or national, a lawful permanent resident, or a foreign national authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for employer sponsorship. Employees must maintain work authorization without sponsorship for the duration of their appointment. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) 8:00am-4:30pm, Monday-Friday About St. Cloud State University serves close to 10,000 students and is committed to providing accessible, high-quality education that prepares graduates for meaningful careers and lifelong success. Located along the Mississippi River in St. Cloud, Minnesota, SCSU combines personalized support, applied learning, research, and community engagement to create opportunities for students, employees, and the region. With more than 133,000 alumni worldwide, SCSU continues to make a lasting impact through education, innovation, and service. St. Cloud State University is committed to creating an inclusive and welcoming environment that values the unique contributions of all students, faculty, staff, and community members. We recognize that welcoming a variety of perspectives, experiences, and backgrounds strengthens our teaching, learning, research, and service mission. We encourage applications from individuals who share our commitment to student success, belonging, and excellence. Employment for this position is covered by the collective bargaining agreement for the Minnesota Association of Professional Employees (MAPE) which can be found at: https://mape.org/ St. Cloud State University is committed to excellence and actively supports cultural diversity. To promote this endeavor, we invite individuals who contribute to such diversity to apply, including minorities, women, LGBTQIA+, persons with disabilities and veterans. St. Cloud State University does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, marital status, status with regards to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or status as a U.S. veteran. The Interim Title IX coordinator at St. Cloud State University is Susan Woolf. For additional information, contact the Office of Institutional Equity & Access, (320) 308-5123, Admin. Services Bldg. Rm 121  Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 11-01-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 08-31-2026 Close Date: 09-15-2026 Posting Contact Name: Courtney Marie Graber Posting Contact Email: courtney.graber@stcloudstate.edu"
    },
