      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 7 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Adjunct Cosmetology Instructor Institution: Riverland Community College Classification Title: Community College Faculty Bargaining Unit / Union: 218: Non-Unit City: Austin FLSA: Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Part time Employment Condition: Unclassified - Limited Academic (Fixed Term) Salary Range: $44,359.00 - $101,620.00 Job Description: We are seeking an instructor dedicated to excellence in teaching who desires to make a difference in the lives of our students. This teaching assignment is located on the Austin Campus. The instructor will be assigned to teach in a traditional classroom and lab format. Activities related to comprehensive community college teaching and learning, including but not limited to: Instructional planning and delivery; Teaching and facilitating student learning; Curriculum planning and development; Assessment of student performance; Classroom management; Maintenance of professional skills and credentials; Participation in department meetings, coordination activities, and college-wide committees The candidate must be able to work cooperatively with faculty and staff, demonstrate knowledge of and experience in assessing student learning outcomes, participate in department meetings and college-wide committees, and maintain ongoing professional development activities. Salary Range: Part-time faculty members are paid by number of credits taught each semester, and the amount per credit ranges from $775.00-$2,396.43 (depending on education and experience). Minimum Qualifications Education Requirement Diploma in cosmetology Occupational Experience Requirement Four full-time years (or equivalent) of verified related paid work experience as a cosmetologist Recency Requirement One year of this work experience shall be within the five years immediately preceding the date of application for the credential field. The recency requirement shall be waived if the individual has two years of successful full-time (or equivalent) postsecondary teaching experience in the credential field within the last five years. Professional Requirement Cosmetology instructor license from the Minnesota Board of Cosmetology Examiners Preferred Qualifications Bilingual/multilingual fluent in Spanish, Karen, Karenni, Somali, Pohnpeian, French, Nuer, Anuak, or other languages that reflect our student body, workforce, and communities. Demonstrated experience working with multicultural and underserved populations. Other Requirements: A complete online application will include a letter of interest and resume/curriculum vitae. Please note that the search committee will not review incomplete applications. This position requires completing employment references and a driver’s license background check. Minnesota State is unable to sponsor Applicants for work visas. All Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the US. If you would like to request an accommodation as part of the application process, please contact Aimee Sue Larson at aimee.larson@riverland.edu Work Shift (Hours / Days of work): Part-time; varies based on student need Telework (Yes/No) No About: Riverland Community College is dedicated to fostering an environment where employees, students, and the region thrive. Guided by our vision, mission, and values, we provide excellent opportunities for students to reach their academic and career goals. Our values focus on cultivating student growth through service, collaboration, innovation, and respect. We offer a supportive and innovative culture that values individual and team contributions and is committed to diversity and inclusion. Diversity and Inclusion : We are dedicated to continually developing a workforce that mirrors the diversity of our students and communities. We recognize the value of diverse experiences and perspectives, which enhance our ability to serve the people of our region effectively. Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) Commitment: Riverland is an emerging Hispanic-Serving Institution. We welcome candidates who understand HSIs and the Latinx student experience, further enriching our inclusive community. Student-Centered Education: With small class sizes, personalized instruction, and hands-on learning. Riverland offers student-centered education that empowers individuals to succeed. Our diverse range of credit and non-credit courses caters to various learning modalities. Program Offerings : With campuses in Albert Lea, Austin, and Owatonna, Riverland offers associate degrees in over 90 career options, liberal arts and sciences, and customized training, providing comprehensive educational opportunities for all. Community and Quality of Life: Located in southern Minnesota, our region boasts excellent public and parochial education systems, diverse recreational activities for all seasons, and upscale communities that enrich personal and professional lives. Join Riverland Community College, where dedication to employees, students, and the region drives excellence in education and service. To learn more about Riverland or Minnesota State, visit www.riverland.edu or www.minnstate.edu. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 09-17-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 08-28-2026 Close Date: 06-30-2027 Posting Contact Name: Mary Ellen Greeley Abdo Posting Contact Email: Mary.Abdo@riverland.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Mankato/Director-of-Curriculum-Management---Management-Analyst-3--AA26153-_JR0000005446": {
      "title": "Director of Curriculum Management - Management Analyst 3 (AA26153)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Director of Curriculum Management - Management Analyst 3 (AA26153) Institution: Minnesota State University, Mankato Classification Title: Management Analyst 3 Bargaining Unit / Union: 214: Minnesota Association of Professional Employees City: Mankato FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Classified - Unlimited Salary Range: $28.75 - $42.16 Salary Range: $28.75 - $42.16 / hourly; $60,030 - $88,030 / annually Job Description The Director of Curriculum Management provides leadership, coordination, and oversight of the university’s curriculum development and approval processes. This position ensures the accuracy, integrity, and consistency of academic program information across all institutional systems, supports faculty and academic units in developing and revising curricula with an equity lens, and serves as the central point of contact for curriculum policy, governance workflows, and compliance requirements. The Director collaborates closely with Academic Affairs, Registrar’s Office, Institutional Research, accreditation teams, and academic colleges to ensure that curriculum processes are efficient, transparent, and aligned with institutional goals and regulatory standards. The position supports departments with market research and viability analysis to inform decisions about new and existing academic programs. Through strong communication, project management, and collaboration, the Director ensures that curriculum processes are efficient, compliant, and supportive of institutional goals. Minimum Qualifications Substantial experience (three or more years) in curriculum development, academic planning, or academic program management in a higher education setting.  Demonstrated ability to apply an equity lens to program and curriculum design, academic portfolio management, and analysis of demand for academic programs. Strong project management skills, including the ability to manage complex initiatives, coordinate across departments, and meet institutional deadlines.  Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, including the ability to collaborate with diverse stakeholders including faculty, staff, and administrators; to present complex information clearly and concisely; and to develop recommendations and technical reports for non-technical users and for specialist users as appropriate. Experience with curriculum management systems, academic planning tools, student information systems, and large databases and the ability to guide their effective use across the institution.  Demonstrated ability to analyze and communicate curriculum-related data to inform executive decision-making and long-term academic planning, including market analysis and recommendations for curriculum development. Demonstrated ability to interpret and apply academic policies, accreditation standards, and regulatory requirements related to curriculum and program development. Preferred Qualification  Master’s or doctoral degree in any discipline (Conferred on an official transcript at the time of application). Demonstrated commitment to fostering a diverse working and learning environment. Demonstrated success in facilitating professional development or institutional training related to curriculum design, academic planning, or program review. Familiarity with the Minnesota State Colleges and Universities system, including ISRS or Workday, and system-level curriculum policies and procedures. Knowledge of state, federal, and accrediting body requirements for academic programs at all levels (undergraduate, graduate, and professional). Experience managing or supporting transitions in academic systems, such as student information systems or catalog platforms. Other Requirements Please note that successful applicants must be eligible to work in the United States on or before the effective date of appointment. Eligibility includes being a U.S. citizen or national, a lawful permanent resident, or a foreign national authorized to work in the U.S. without the need for employer sponsorship. Employees must maintain work authorization without sponsorship for the duration of their appointment. Work safely at all times, which includes but is not limited to, participating and completing all required safety trainings, as well as performing all job tasks in accordance with Minnesota State University, Mankato policies and procedures utilizing appropriate tools, equipment and personal protective equipment. The Minnesota State University, Mankato Annual Security and Fire Safety Report is available for your review. This report is required by federal law and contains policy statements and crime statistics for the University. The policy statements address the school’s policies, procedures and programs concerning safety and security. Three years’ worth of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that were reported to have occurred on-campus, or in other University affiliated locations. This report is available online at: http://www.mnsu.edu/safety/ . You may also request a paper copy from University Security at 507-389-2111, or by emailing security@mnsu.edu . Minimal travel required. Up to 5% of the time. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Monday - Friday, 8:00 - 4:30 PM Telework (Yes/No) Yes - Up to 95% of the time. Based on the essential functions of this positions, MMB Policy #1422, and University policies relating to flexible work, this position is eligible for the following work modes: Telework: A position with a work arrangement that allows an employee to perform work on a regular basis at a telework location that is not the employee’s permanent/principal work location. About More than 1600 talented faculty, staff, and 1600 student employees with a wide variety of skills and backgrounds, support university operations every day. Our faculty and staff enjoy excellent benefits, a team environment and challenging careers. As an affirmative action/equal opportunity institution, we are committed to supporting the continued growth of our diverse community. Destination 2030 , the University’s strategic plan announced by President Edward Inch in August 2023, commits the University to making transformative strides in four main areas: being a lifelong provider of access to an equitable and affordable education; being a leader in transformational learning generating inspired action; being a nimble and innovative steward of resources; and being a community of care built upon diversity, inclusion, and belonging. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 12-02-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 08-17-2026 Close Date: 09-29-2026 Posting Contact Name: Sarith Phan Posting Contact Email: sarith.phan@mnsu.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Rochester/Groundskeeper_JR0000005634": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Groundskeeper Institution: Rochester Community and Technical College Classification Title: Groundskeeper Bargaining Unit / Union: 203: AFSCME - Service City: Rochester FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Classified - Unlimited Salary Range: $20.87 - $29.73 Job Description This position is responsible for maintaining, preparing, and caring for Rochester Community and Technical College grounds, athletic fields, lawns, landscaped areas, sidewalks, parking lots, driveways, roads, and other exterior areas. The position performs routine groundskeeping and landscape maintenance, snow and ice removal, operation and maintenance of grounds equipment, and general exterior facility maintenance. The position helps ensure that College grounds and athletic facilities are safe, clean, functional, and attractive for students, employees, visitors, athletic participants, and the public. Salary Range: 20.87 - 29.73 USD Hourly Minimum Qualifications Basic horticultural techniques and practices, including planting, pruning, watering, fertilizing, seeding, sodding, and general lawn and garden care. Methods of lawn, landscape, and athletic field maintenance. Operation and routine maintenance of motorized groundskeeping equipment and hand tools. Basic construction and repair methods sufficient to construct or repair simple structures and grounds features. Methods and equipment used for snow and ice removal. Safe work practices related to groundskeeping, equipment operation, outdoor work, and use of tools and machinery. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualification  Previous experience in groundskeeping, landscaping, turf management, athletic field or sports facility maintenance, or institutional/commercial property maintenance. Experience operating riding mowers, tractors, loaders, snow removal equipment, utility vehicles, or similar equipment. Experience performing routine preventive maintenance and minor repairs on groundskeeping equipment. Experience with irrigation systems and related grounds maintenance. Good human relations skills, work habits, and self-motivation. Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) 8:00am-4:30pm, Tuesday-Saturday Telework (Yes/No) No About RCTC is a member of Minnesota State- a higher education system that includes 24 two-year community and technical colleges and seven state universities serving more than 430,000 students. It is the fifth-largest higher education system of its kind in the United States. Working together to improve the state we love.  What do Minnesota's State employees have in common?  A sense of purpose in their work Connection with their coworkers and communities Opportunities for personal and professional growth Benefits  As an employee, you'll have access to one of the most affordable health insurance plans in Minnesota, along with other benefits to help you and your family be well. Your benefits may include:  Paid vacation and sick leave  12 paid holidays each year  Low-cost medical, dental, vision, and prescription drug plans  Fertility care, including IVF Diabetes care Dental and orthodontic care for adults and children  6 weeks paid leave for parents of newborn or newly adopted children Pension plan that provides income when you retire (after working at least three years) Employer paid life insurance to provide support for your family in the event of death Short-term and long-term disability insurance that can provide income if you are unable to work due to illness or injury Tax-free expense accounts for health, dental, and dependent care  Resources that provide support and promote physical, emotional, social, and financial well-being Support to help you reach your career goals: Training, classes, and professional development Tuition reimbursement  Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program (Some positions may qualify for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program. For more information, visit the Federal Student Aid website at studentaid.gov ) Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for work/life support: A voluntary confidential program that helps employees and their families with life challenges that may impact overall health, personal well-being, or job performance Common sources of stress can be addressed through the EAP: mental health, relationship challenges (personal and work), grief and loss, finances, and legal issues Daily Living/Convenience Services: Chore services, home repair, trip planning, child/elder care Programs, resources and benefits eligibility varies based on type of employment, agency, funding availability, union/collective bargaining agreement, location, and length of service with the State of Minnesota.  Other Information  Employment information for this position can be found in its collective bargaining agreement or its plan document at http://mn.gov/mmb/employee-relations/labor-relations/Labor/. Non-Discrimination/Equal Opportunity Rochester Community and Technical College acts affirmatively in aggressively soliciting applications and hiring members of protected groups, including women, minorities, veterans, and disabled persons. We apply equal opportunity in our hiring process and provide reasonable accommodation upon request. Persons in protected classes are encouraged to apply. Please assist us in this affirmative action endeavor by encouraging all qualified candidates to apply for vacancies at our institution. NOTICE: In accordance with the Minnesota State Colleges & Universities Vehicle Fleet Safety Program, employees driving on college/university business, whether using a personal, rental or state vehicle, shall be required to conform to Minnesota State’s vehicle use criteria and consent to a Motor Vehicle Records check. The safety of all members of the Rochester Community and Technical College campus community is of vital concern. Resources including the current Annual Security Report are available at our  Campus Safety webpage . AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER  Minnesota State is an equal opportunity employer/educator committed to the principles of diversity. We prohibit discrimination against qualified individuals based on their race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, marital status, status with regard to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or membership in a local commission as defined by law. As an affirmative action employer, we actively seek and encourage applications from women, minorities, persons with disabilities, and individuals with protected veteran status. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 09-11-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 08-27-2026 Close Date: Posting Contact Name: Haley Marie Lenway Posting Contact Email:"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/MWST---Pipestone-Campus/Student-Services-Specialist---Customer-Svc-Special-Intermed_JR0000005308": {
      "title": "Student Services Specialist - Customer Svc Special Intermed",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: Student Services Specialist - Customer Svc Special Intermed Institution: Minnesota West Community and Technical College Classification Title: Customer Svcs Specialist Int Bargaining Unit / Union: 206: AFSCME - Clerical and Office City: MWST - Pipestone Campus FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Part time Employment Condition: Classified - Unlimited Salary Range: $21.12 - $29.73 Job Description: This position provides exemplary customer services and support to both internal and external constituents and provides timely, accurate, and detailed information to prospective and current students, to help the College reach its enrollment goals.  The position requires a strong working knowledge of all service areas of admissions, advising, registration and financial aid and is expected to work collaboratively with all Student Services and Student Support offices on more in-depth inquiries for resolution.  The Student Support Specialist requires a high level of professional customer service and knowledge in order to research, investigate, and resolve both simple and complex student issues under minimal supervision, regularly exercising professional judgement and discretion on individual student cases.  This includes providing complicated and specialized information regarding policies and procedures in high-pressure, high-volume situations.  This position includes additional specialized project work and administrative support, based on the need of Office of Student Services and Enrollment. Administrative support, which may include but is not limited to data entry, management of student files and records.  This position has direct responsibility for understanding process from the start of the college application to graduation, which requires extensive knowledge of Minnesota State and Minnesota West policy and procedures, technical skills, and great attention to details.  All employees, on a daily basis, are expected to execute a service commitment to ensure all students are served and have a positive experience. Serves as the primary customer service liaison within the Office of Student Services and Enrollment.  Maintains a thorough and comprehensive understanding of the College’s admissions processes, college programs, support services and resources and provides clear and concise responses to requests for information and assistance from external customers.  Direct students and families to resources needed to navigate the overall college experience.  Aid with appointment scheduling, online application, financial aid, eServices, and more.  Use specialized knowledge to provide problem resolution for more difficult or more involved, complicated, and controversial issues.  Final answer and resolution of problems frequently require outreach and repeated discussions/interviews with the customer.  Follow-up with students or staff as needed to ensure proper resolution of the issue.  Exercise initiative in resolving situations not requiring the Dean or Director‘s personal attention - only escalate situations as appropriate.  Treat all issues with integrity and confidentiality.  Serve as front line in financial aid completion, tracking letter completion, loan counseling, and understanding of awarding of aid. Educate, guide, and ability to apply state and college policies related to bills, payment, financial aid, code of conduct, grievance, satisfactory academic progress, registration holds, and credit limit. Schedule, coordinate, and support group and individual campus visits, tours, and other recruitment events for prospective students and their families. Plan, schedule, coordinate, and support graduation and retention activities and events. Provide comprehensive support to students, families, employees, campus visitors and external clientele. Perform quality assurance and administrative support to ensure accurate and timely processing of student records and campus operations. Verify, organize, image and maintain the accuracy of data entered into student records using systems such as Workday, ISRS, EAB/Navigate Student Success & Enrollment Success, and Perceptive Content. Assist in mitigating student fraud through ID and student information verification. Conduct student outreach campaigns and follow-up communications to support application, registration, appointments, and other student requirements while providing professional, accurate, and courteous customer service. Provide campus administrative support by managing mail and shipping, maintaining office, event, and student basic needs supplies, and coordinating EMS event scheduling, contracts, and campus event planning. Business Office Support Provide accounting support to the campus in the form of receipting, and cash management in preparation for deposit. Coordinate collections with college business office by identifying student’s deferments, agency funding, etc. Trouble shooting errors on student’s accounts and monitor the Department of Finance for electronic funds transfer and process appropriately. Reconcile local bank account monthly. Sell merchandise in the campus store. Other business office functions as assigned. Other duties as assigned Provide additional support to the Office of Student Service and Enrollment through specialized tasks and projects, such as but not limited to student worker supervision, completing requisitions, uploading receipts, outreach to vendors, etc. and communicating to the college. Participate in work group discussion for mapping business processes, measuring improvement and coordinating work for continuous improvement of processes and procedure related to Student Services and Enrollment. Perform other duties as assigned to ensure the smooth functional of the department and maintain the reputation of the organization as a viable business partner.         Salary Range: $21.12 - $29.73 per hour. Part-time; 37.50 hours per week. This position requires working on-site at the Pipestone campus. Remote work or hybrid work arrangements are not available for this position. Minimum Qualifications Skill in customer service sufficient to provide prompt and accurate information to customers in person, on the phone, and through email and other written or electronic correspondence. Ability to respectfully engage with clients, coworkers, and customers, when handling difficult or complex problems and resolving escalated complaints or disputes. Ability to answer questions and advise customers of program policies, procedures, and regulations. Knowledge of standard computer software programs for word processing, spreadsheets, and databases sufficient to create, modify, and protect files. Skill in document and records management sufficient to maintain electronic or paper files for efficient organization and retrieval of information. Ability to analyze and make recommendations to management for new or revised administrative and program practices and procedures for smooth and efficient office operation. Skill in basic accounting sufficient to identify and resolve discrepancies in accounting records. Preferred Qualification  Translating from Spanish to English to sufficient to meet clients, co-workers, and customer’s needs. Knowledge of admissions, registration and financial aid procedures and services sufficient to answer student, staff, and the public’s questions. Knowledge of Minnesota West programs, policies, services, and procedures sufficient to answer questions asked and refer other questions appropriately. Skilled in using MS Office (Outlook, Word, Excel, and Access), online chat or instant messaging applications, customer relationship management software, or Minnesota State ISRS database. Knowledge of FERPA and Minnesota Government Data Practices Act and the ability to maintain the confidentiality of private information in compliance with laws, policies, and procedures. Demonstrated initiative to trouble-shoot and correct incomplete and complicated situations Other Requirements You must apply online and attach an electronic cover letter and resume to your online application in order to be considered for this position. ​All applicants must be able to lawfully accept employment in the United States at the time of employment.  ​In accordance with the Minnesota State Vehicle Fleet Safety Program, employees driving on college/university business who use a rental or state vehicle shall be required to conform to Minnesota State's vehicle use criteria and consent to a Motor Vehicle Records check ​ Work Shift (Hours / Days of work) Monday - Friday; 37.50 hours per week. Telework (Yes/No) No. This position requires onsite work and is not eligible for telework or remote work. About Minnesota West Community and Technical College is a student-centered, open-access community and technical college within the Minnesota State Colleges and Universities system. The college provides transfer, occupational and career programs, workforce training, educational outreach and life-long learning opportunities. The College is committed to accomplishing its mission: Dedicated to serving the varied educational needs of our diverse populations in affordable, accessible and supportive settings. Minnesota West Community and Technical College is a comprehensive community and technical college with five southwestern Minnesota campuses: Canby, Granite Falls, Jackson, Pipestone, and Worthington and learning centers in Luverne and Marshall Minnesota. Students have the opportunity to earn an Associate Degree, Diploma, or Certificate in more than 60 disciplines.   Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 10-01-2026 Position End Date: Open Date: 07-20-2026 Close Date: 09-11-2026 Posting Contact Name: Tricia Bueltel Posting Contact Email: tricia.bueltel@mnwest.edu"
    },
    "https://minnstate.wd115.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Rochester/General-Maintenance-Worker_JR0000004917": {
      "title": "General Maintenance Worker",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nAll Job Postings will close at 12:01 a.m. CT on the specified Closing Date (if designated). Working Title: General Maintenance Worker Institution: Rochester Community and Technical College Classification Title: General Maintenance Wrkr Bargaining Unit / Union: 203: AFSCME - Service City: Rochester FLSA: Non Job Exempt Full Time / Part Time: Full time Employment Condition: Classified - Unlimited Salary Range: $20.87 - $29.73 Job Description: This position is responsible for cleaning and general maintenance services throughout the campus. This position shall provide a safe, clean environment for visitors, faculty, staff, and students.  This position will assist with snow removal and landscaping duties and may also perform delivery/receiving operations on campus and assist the mail room as necessary. This position shall assist in the safety, security, maintenance, and operations of Rochester Community and Technical College to ensure the College operates in a clean, safe and secure environment.   Salary Range: $20.51-$25.43 Minimum Qualifications: Knowledge of:  Different types of flooring/floor coverings sufficient to determine proper methods of maintenance and appropriate cleaning methods, materials, agents and equipment. Chemical cleaning agents such as ammonia, bleaches, scouring agents and soaps sufficient to appropriately select the agent(s), handle and apply, and dispose of safely. Methods, tools, and equipment used in maintenance sufficient to use effectively and operate safely and to make minor repairs.  Ability to: Follow oral and written instructions.   Perform assigned tasks with limited work direction.   Keep adequate records. Physical health and endurance are sufficient to perform work functions: Ability to perform work functions using ladders, scaffolding, etc.   Ability to lift and carry up to 30 lbs. regularly and 30-50 lbs. on occasion (with assistance as available).   Capable of frequent standing, walking, lifting, carrying, pushing, and pulling and repetitive activities such as standing, walking, lifting, bending, reaching, carrying, pushing and pulling. Preferred Qualification: Ability to use hand tools Good human relations skills, work habits, and self-motivation Valid Driver’s License Work Shift (Hours / Days of work): Friday-Monday 12:00 p.m.-10:30 p.m. Telework (Yes/No): No About: RCTC is a member of Minnesota State- a higher education system that includes 24 two-year community and technical colleges and seven state universities serving more than 430,000 students. It is the fifth-largest higher education system of its kind in the United States. Working together to improve the state we love.  What do Minnesota's State employees have in common?  A sense of purpose in their work Connection with their coworkers and communities Opportunities for personal and professional growth Benefits  As an employee, you'll have access to one of the most affordable health insurance plans in Minnesota, along with other benefits to help you and your family be well. Your benefits may include:  Paid vacation and sick leave  12 paid holidays each year  Low-cost medical, dental, vision, and prescription drug plans  Fertility care, including IVF Diabetes care Dental and orthodontic care for adults and children  6 weeks paid leave for parents of newborn or newly adopted children Pension plan that provides income when you retire (after working at least three years) Employer paid life insurance to provide support for your family in the event of death Short-term and long-term disability insurance that can provide income if you are unable to work due to illness or injury Tax-free expense accounts for health, dental, and dependent care  Resources that provide support and promote physical, emotional, social, and financial well-being Support to help you reach your career goals: Training, classes, and professional development Tuition reimbursement  Federal Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program (Some positions may qualify for the Public Service Loan Forgiveness Program. For more information, visit the Federal Student Aid website at studentaid.gov ) Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for work/life support: A voluntary confidential program that helps employees and their families with life challenges that may impact overall health, personal well-being, or job performance Common sources of stress can be addressed through the EAP: mental health, relationship challenges (personal and work), grief and loss, finances, and legal issues Daily Living/Convenience Services: Chore services, home repair, trip planning, child/elder care Programs, resources and benefits eligibility varies based on type of employment, agency, funding availability, union/collective bargaining agreement, location, and length of service with the State of Minnesota.  Other Information  Employment information for this position can be found in its collective bargaining agreement or its plan document at http://mn.gov/mmb/employee-relations/labor-relations/Labor/. Non-Discrimination/Equal Opportunity Rochester Community and Technical College acts affirmatively in aggressively soliciting applications and hiring members of protected groups, including women, minorities, veterans, and disabled persons. We apply equal opportunity in our hiring process and provide reasonable accommodation upon request. Persons in protected classes are encouraged to apply. Please assist us in this affirmative action endeavor by encouraging all qualified candidates to apply for vacancies at our institution. NOTICE: In accordance with the Minnesota State Colleges & Universities Vehicle Fleet Safety Program, employees driving on college/university business, whether using a personal, rental or state vehicle, shall be required to conform to Minnesota State’s vehicle use criteria and consent to a Motor Vehicle Records check. The safety of all members of the Rochester Community and Technical College campus community is of vital concern. Resources including the current Annual Security Report are available at our  Campus Safety webpage . AN EQUAL OPPORTUNITY EMPLOYER  Minnesota State is an equal opportunity employer/educator committed to the principles of diversity. We prohibit discrimination against qualified individuals based on their race, sex, color, creed, religion, age, national origin, disability, protected veteran status, marital status, status with regard to public assistance, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, or membership in a local commission as defined by law. As an affirmative action employer, we actively seek and encourage applications from women, minorities, persons with disabilities, and individuals with protected veteran status. Benefits Information: At Minnesota State, we take your well-being and work-life balance seriously. We offer a comprehensive benefits package that features low-cost medical and dental insurance with affordable deductibles, employer-paid life insurance, short- and long-term disability, and pre-tax healthcare and dependent care accounts with a roll-over option. To further support your holistic health, employees also have access to a confidential Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for mental health, legal, and financial counseling. Detailed plan details, rates, and coverage choices can be reviewed directly via the State Employee Group Insurance Program (SEGIP) website.   To support your life outside of work, our package includes 12 paid holidays, generous vacation and sick time, and six weeks of Paid Parental Leave. We also help you secure your financial future with a robust Pension Plan, 457(b) and 403(b) retirement accounts, and various investment options. Furthermore, we invest in your growth by providing dedicated professional development and tuition waivers for both you and your dependents. Please note that specific benefit eligibility and coverage levels may vary depending on the type of position, employee classification, and collective bargaining agreements. Desired Start Date: 09-18-2026 Position End Date: 09-19-2026 Open Date: 05-20-2026 Close Date: 09-18-2026 Posting Contact Name: Kris Kohn Posting Contact Email: kris.kohn@rctc.edu"
