eractions with students. This is a Monday – Friday position during the academic year. Salary Range: $22.27 -$31.12 hourly Minimum Qualifications Post-secondary or industry certificate/diploma/degree and relevant licensure in Registered Nursing AND One year of training/teaching/tutoring experience in Nursing at the high school level or above Preferred Qualification  Evidence of commitment to the success of culturally, ethnically, and racially diverse populations of students, staff, and faculty. Demonstrated understanding of academic/developmental needs of non-traditional students, including non-native speakers of English, students with disabilities, first generation college students, and post-traditional generation students for use in tutoring online and in-person, utilizing active and student-centered learning techniques. Interpersonal and communication skills, including listening, speaking, writing, and the ability to interact professionally with diverse populations in a positive, courteous, and helpful manner Organizational and detail-oriented skills to collaboratively maintain the operations of the lab Ability to learn the latest in nursing technology and relate this new learning to nursing students Experience in nursing care in a variety of environments and willingness to learn about application in simulation and tutoring for lab and lecture. Familiar with technology such as Electronic Medical Records (EMR), Word, Power Point, D2L Brightspace or similar software Other Requirements Please complete the online application form and upload these documents by the posting deadline. This position is posted through August 25, 2026. The posting will be removed from the website on September 22, 2026 12:01 am central time.  Cover Letter Resume Within your application material, please address how you meet all minimum qualifications and any preferred qualifications for this position. Incomplete applications may not be accepted. Internal Applicants All current Minnesota State 